Replace this with a real capability. The frontmatter is the validated data; this body
is the "why" — the reason someone should build it, in a paragraph a person will read.

Two things here are load-bearing. `about` must resolve to a real term id. And each
`tests` entry must name a test that actually exists: rename
`test_the_example_holds_for_empty_input` and `keelspec validate` fails with
**PAC-902** before anyone reviews the PR.

The second criterion has no test, which is allowed — until `status` becomes
`shipped`, at which point it is **PAC-900**. Drafting without proof is fine; shipping
without it is the thing the gate exists to stop.
